WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.452
IS DISTINCT FROM is useful in cleaning updates because it handles NULL explicitly.

00:00:04.452 --> 00:00:07.512
Ordinary equality follows three-valued logic.

00:00:07.512 --> 00:00:13.567
IS DISTINCT FROM tells you whether two values are meaningfully different, including cases where one is NULL.

00:00:13.567 --> 00:00:18.457
This can help avoid unnecessary updates and make conditions more predictable.

00:00:18.457 --> 00:00:23.817
Connect this idea to a customer master-data project cleaning duplicate profiles.

00:00:23.817 --> 00:00:28.587
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:28.587 --> 00:00:35.272
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:35.272 --> 00:00:40.237
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:40.237 --> 00:00:45.280
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
